course: dictionary
lesson: 162
title: One short word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word ag has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is right. Look for clues first. «Ag school» and «ag science» are about farming, because ag is short for agriculture, the work of farming.
explain: In a science lesson, Ag with a capital A and a small g means silver. It is a chemical symbol, from the Latin name argentum. Capital letters matter here, so look at how the word is written.
explain: In South African English, «Ag, man!» is an exclamation, like "oh" or "ugh". It shows annoyance, sympathy or giving up, and it is said with a throaty sound like "ach". Ask yourself: is the speaker cross, sorry for someone, or giving up?
fact: Ag has three meanings: farming (short for agriculture), silver (a chemical symbol), and an exclamation in South African English.
fact: «Ag school» and «ag science» are about farming.
fact: Ag with a capital A and a small g is the chemical symbol for silver, with atomic number 47.
fact: In South African English, «ag» shows mild annoyance, and «just now» can mean later.
fact: Capital letters help: Ag (silver) is written with a capital A and small g, but the other meanings are often written in small letters.
exercise: «She joined the ag club to learn how to grow wheat.» What does ag mean here? | An exclamation of annoyance | *Agriculture, the work of farming | A type of bird | Silver, the metal
exercise: In a science test, the periodic table shows Ag. What does it stand for? | Gold | Farming | *Silver | An exclamation
exercise: «Ag, man! The bus left without me.» What feeling does ag show? | Happy surprise | Farming | *Annoyance | Silver
test: «Ag, man, I missed the bus again!» What does the ag show? | Farming | Joy | Silver | *Annoyance
test: Which symbol is the chemical symbol for silver? | Si | Au | *Ag | Ar
exam: «Ag» can mean farming, silver or an exclamation. How can you tell which one is meant? | Ag never changes its meaning, so any answer is fine | Ask a friend to guess | *Read the context: science words point to silver, farm words point to farming, and a cross or sorry feeling points to the exclamation | Always choose farming, because it is the most common
